Z||000011||ToddAsh||12-13-2001||10:06 PM|||| I just replaced my heater core at 17,000 original miles.Had a little corrosion hole in the inlet pipe but the core looked perfect.Replaced it anyway while it was out.Have two V6 Fieros,took the cat off my '85 V6 SE and it is definitly quicker than my '86 GT. Other than that they are identical.The only problem is it's a little too loud.Used Rodney Dickman's pipe.Going to put one of the insert mufflers from Jeg's ($42) into the cat pipe when I'm off 2 weeks for Christmas.One of several Fiero projects I've got lined up for then.||||reg||1
Z||000012||deceler8||12-14-2001||09:06 AM||||Heater core replacement is a breeze. Had to do it two weeks ago.<P>And I was really dreading it, even though everyone here claimed it was an hour or less job.<P>But, sure enough, it was an hour or less job.<P>The problem with just rerouting the heater hoses to see if the core leaks is that if it has been leaking for any period of time the whole system will have coolant spread through it which will need to dry out.<P>And when you do change it, be sure to have plenty of towels underneath the housing because the housing will hold a lot of coolant before any leaks are evident.||||reg||1
Z||000013||NEPTUNE||12-14-2001||09:24 AM||||You definitely have a leaky heater core. replacement is not difficult.<BR>PLEASE do not run without a cat- You will not see any gain in performance, you will only add unnecessary pollution to our already saturated atmosphere. If there were a big gain in performance, I could see doing it, but there is no gain. You can buy an aftermarket cat for approx $55(usd) that will flow better than the stock one.  ||||reg||4
